    <p>After many warnings, the book of Amos closes with a promise: God will raise up the fallen booth (house) of David, repair its breaches, restore the fortunes of His people, and plant them in their land never to be uprooted again (paraphrase of 9:11–15). The land will be so fruitful that the ploughman will overtake the reaper.</p>
